Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:07:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s8003: Describe the GPU
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The A9's GPU: the Rogue core's registers, Fender, the gfx power domain
and the five interrupts, and the firmware the driver loads (the image
the firmware recipe extracts from the device's kernelcache). The node is
disabled: no driver takes it yet. The powervr driver's Apple firmware
path will, and the boards enable it then.

The registers and interrupts are those of Berkay Kösebay's G5P driver
node (orchard #74, 557ef01b), which runs the GPU on the iPad 5 (J71t).
Reworked for the powervr driver: the gpu label, the firmware name, and
no board enables it before that driver binds.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003.dtsi | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003.dtsi
index b515889..1ed521d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s8003.dtsi
@@ -336,3 +336,25 @@
  * the S8003 (APL1022) on 16nm. There are some minor differences
  * such as timing in cpufreq state transistions.
  */
+
+/*
+ * The GPU: a PowerVR Rogue core (GT7600) behind Apple's Fender block, with
+ * Apple's firmware on the core's own processor. Off until a driver takes it.
+ */
+&{/soc} {
+	gpu: gpu@201000000 {
+		compatible = "apple,s8003-gpu";
+		reg = <0x2 0x01000000 0x0 0x100000>,
+		      <0x2 0x01e00000 0x0 0x100000>;
+		reg-names = "rgx", "fender";
+		power-domains = <&ps_gfx>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+		interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 170 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			     <AIC_IRQ 171 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			     <AIC_IRQ 172 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			     <AIC_IRQ 173 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+			     <AIC_IRQ 174 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		firmware-name = "apple/gfx-s8003.bin";
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+};
